From 0b4fcefec4b46dfdb1931d102e93a85e15c4a30a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Suraj P Kizhakkethil <suraj.kizhakkethil@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Nov 2025 17:26:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:iw: Add support for UHR in set bitrate
 command
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add support for UHR rates and UHR UEQM pattern in set bitrate command.
The command format follows the same structure as EHT, with an
additional optional argument UEQMP, which specifies the UEQM pattern
to use. If this argument is not provided, the rates follow EQM.

Draft P802.11bn_D1.4 Table 38-33 and Table 38-34 defines the allowed
combinations of NSS, MCS and UEQM pattern.

Valid UEQM pattern values: 0 to 3
NSS range supporting UEQM: 2 to 4
Valid UEQM pattern values for an NSS: 0 to NSS-1

Allowed MCS values,
When UEQM pattern = 0: MCS = 3, 4, …, 13, 19 and 23
When UEQM pattern = 1 2 or 3: MCS = 5, 6, 8, 9, …, 13, and 23

Command format:
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l<link_id>
 [uhr-mcs-<2.4|5|6> <NSS:MCSx[:UEMP],MCSy[:UEQMP]... | NSS:MCSx-MCSy[:UEQMP]>*]
 [uhr-gi-<2.4|5|6> <0.8|1.6|3.2>]
 [uhr-ltf-<2.4|5|6> <1|2|4>]

Examples:
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l 0 uhr-mcs-6 2:3-10 uhr-gi-6 0.8 uhr-ltf-6 2
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l 0 uhr-mcs-5 2:0
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l 0 uhr-mcs-6 4:8-13:1
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l 0 uhr-mcs-5 4:8:2
iw dev wlan0 set bitrates -l 0 uhr-mcs-5 4:8:2,3:0,5

Change-Id: Iee84ffeeff24691c6ad6af31b5d07c75db2bd3ed
Signed-off-by: Suraj P Kizhakkethil <suraj.kizhakkethil@oss.qualcomm.com>
